The strongest rules recognize O'/D' followed by a short capitalized fragment,
joined Mc-/Mac-/De-/Le-/La- names, and van der names. Spaced particles and
ordinary elisions get smaller values. A separate negative rule recognizes
an explicitly tokenized Cyrillic stress accent. These are approximate
orthographic rules, not a dictionary of particular people or token IDs.
