There is a large positive pulse for an initial HTML declaration, and for
completing 'Concurrently'. Lowercase 'concurrently' gets a smaller pulse,
attenuated in computing contexts. The second-token colon in an initial
'Title:' field is strongly negative. Smaller negative responses cover
comparison, quantity, restriction, proximity and completion vocabulary.
Most other tokens stay near zero. These rules do not explain the remaining
fine-grained lexical and contextual variation.
